{"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Troubleshooting","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Xcode asks to “Trust & Enable” a macro","level":2,"anchor":"Xcode-asks-to-Trust--Enable-a-macro","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are compiler plugins, so the first build in Xcode"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"prompts once per machine to trust the "},{"code":"SwiduxMacros","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" target. Approve it in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"build error’s fix-it or under "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Settings → Packages","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". On CI, pass"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"-skipMacroValidation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"code":"xcodebuild","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead — there’s no one to click the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dialog."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The first build is slow","level":2,"anchor":"The-first-build-is-slow","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux depends on ","type":"text"},{"code":"swift-syntax","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which the macro system compiles from source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on first build (a few minutes on CI-class hardware). It’s cached afterwards;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing is wrong. CI pipelines benefit from caching "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".build\/"},{"type":"text","text":" or DerivedData."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Console-shows-Re-entrant-Storesend-deferring","type":"heading","text":"Console shows “Re-entrant Store.send(…) — deferring”","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Something called "},{"code":"store.send","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" synchronously from inside a reducer or plugin"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hook — usually a plugin observing state and dispatching in "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Binding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" setter fired during view updates. The store defers the inner action"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and runs it as a full cycle right after the current one, so state stays"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consistent — but the fault log is telling you the design wants that follow-up"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dispatched from an "},{"code":"Effect","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"call-to-main-actor-isolated-initializer--in-a-synchronous-nonisolated-context","type":"heading","text":"`call to main actor-isolated initializer … in a synchronous nonisolated context`","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The module is compiling in Swift 5 language mode with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SWIFT_DEFAULT_ACTOR_ISOLATION = MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux nonisolated struct"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only gets a nonisolated synthesized memberwise initializer under ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swift 6","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mode","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SWIFT_VERSION = 6.0"},{"type":"text","text":"); under Swift 5 mode the macro’s state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reconstruction can’t call it, and adding an explicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nonisolated init"},{"type":"text","text":" does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not rescue it. Switch the target to Swift 6 mode."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Error: “stored properties need an explicit type annotation”","anchor":"Error-stored-properties-need-an-explicit-type-annotation","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"var flag = false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives the compiler an inferred type, but macros can’t see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it — before this diagnostic existed, such a property was silently skipped and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its value reset on every dispatch. Write ","type":"text"},{"code":"var flag: Bool = false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"applies to combined declarations: split ","type":"text"},{"code":"var a, b: Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" into separate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declarations.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Keychain writes fail with OSStatus −34018 (`errSecMissingEntitlement`)","anchor":"Keychain-writes-fail-with-OSStatus-%E2%88%9234018-errSecMissingEntitlement","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An unsigned local or CI build is using "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" without a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"provisioning profile. This is a signing condition, not a prompt or a bug — the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"data-protection keychain never prompts. Ship provisioning-profile-signed builds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accessGroup: nil"},{"type":"text","text":"; for unsigned local\/CI builds add a single"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"team-prefixed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"keychain-access-groups"},{"type":"text","text":" entitlement. Details in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Contributors-the-lint-plugin-doesnt-run--dev-tooling-is-missing","type":"heading","text":"Contributors: the lint plugin doesn’t run \/ dev tooling is missing","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dev tooling (the Persnoop linter, the DocC plugin) is gated behind a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gitignored "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dev-tooling"},{"type":"text","text":" sentinel file so it never leaks into consumers’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dependency graphs. Create it at the package root — and if the package was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already built without it, run "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift package purge-cache"},{"type":"text","text":" so SwiftPM re-reads"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the manifest. See the repository’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"CONTRIBUTING.md","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"A `@Persisted` app crashes only in Release","anchor":"A-Persisted-app-crashes-only-in-Release"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the crash is in fetching, make sure you’re on ≥ 1.3.0: generic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#Predicate"},{"type":"text","text":" over a protocol-required keypath traps under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-O"},{"type":"text","text":", which is why"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the macro generates a per-model "},{"code":"swiduxFetchDescriptor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift test -c release"},{"type":"text","text":" in CI to catch this class of issue — Debug builds and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default "},{"code":"swift test","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pass.","type":"text"}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Symptoms you may hit while adopting Swidux, and what each one actually means.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Reference","title":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"],"generated":true}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/troubleshooting"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/KeyValueStoreGuide":{"kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","title":"KeyValueStore","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/keyvaluestoreguide","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist scalar preferences like theme, sort order, or last-seen version — testably, with type-safe keys."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginParentalGateReference":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginparentalgatereference","abstract":[{"text":"API surface for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library